    "narrative": "For today\u2019s slate, **Jos\u00e9 Ram\u00edrez** (79.71) serves as our cornerstone play despite a nagging 36% rain risk in his matchup against Montero. His combination of an elite base projection and a favorable matchup against a starter with a 4.51 xERA makes him an auto-start, though he must be monitored closely for delays. Meanwhile, **Tyler Freeman** (65.79) earns a high-floor rating against Tyler Alexander; his aggressive 14% park factor boost makes him an unexpectedly strong play, even with a 45% rain risk hovering over his contest. Both **Will Smith** (65.59) and **Jung Hoo Lee** (62.55) benefit from clear platoon or order advantages, with **Jung Hoo Lee** effectively maximizing his value as a leadoff man against Ryne Nelson, whose 4.12 xERA offers a exploitable target for our top-of-the-order speed assets.\n\nOur most difficult roster decision involved **Jonathan Aranda**, who landed just outside the starting nine with a 47.17 score. While **Jonathan Aranda** benefits from a strong xwOBA profile, the optimizer relegated him to the bench in favor of the higher-upside profiles of **Gavin Sheets** and **Drew Gilbert** due to lingering park factor concerns at his venue. We are also proceeding with caution regarding **Bryson Stott** (53.35) and **Gavin Sheets** (41.89); both face elite arms (Burns and Emmet Sheehan, respectively) who suppress scoring metrics significantly, resulting in a 19% penalty to their base projections. We will rely on the stolen base potential of **Masyn Winn** and the versatility of **Daulton Varsho** to bridge the gap if our power bats struggle against these tougher SP matchups. We remain attentive to official lineups, as several of our starters\u2014specifically **Will Smith**, **Luis Arraez**, **Masyn Winn**, **Geraldo Perdomo**, **Jung Hoo Lee**, **Daulton Varsho**, **Gavin Sheets**, **Drew Gilbert**, and **Matt Chapman**\u2014are currently projected based on historical batting order assumptions.",
